  Content: 'A noodle dish orginating from the canals of Thailand. Usually containing
    pork or beef in a thick soup seasoned with pig or cow blood and spices.


    Many products - especially natural ingredients - became scarce after the city
    of Agartha went into lockdown. It is thanks to the tencity of the immigrant cooks
    and growers that these culinary traditions have been kept alive. '
